course: dictionary
lesson: 6087
title: Space rocks: meteoroid, meteor, meteorite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A meteorite is a piece of rock or metal from space that has landed on the Earth's surface. Scientists use three names for the same space rock, depending on where it is.
explain: «A space rock is a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air and a meteorite if a piece lands on the ground.» So the word tells you the rock's position: still in space, burning in the air, or lying on the ground.
explain: Meteorites are often heavy because they contain iron. Many are older than the Earth itself. If a sentence says a piece has landed, the word you want is meteorite.
fact: A meteoroid is a small rock travelling in space.
fact: A meteor is the streak of light, often called a shooting star, when it glows as it burns in our air.
fact: A meteorite is the piece that reaches the ground.
fact: «Most meteorites are chips of asteroids from the belt between Mars and Jupiter.»
fact: A giant meteorite hit the Earth about 66 million years ago and helped wipe out the dinosaurs.
exercise: «A space rock is a meteoroid in space, a meteor while it glows in the air and a meteorite if a piece lands on the ground.» What is a meteorite? | *A piece of rock or metal from space that has landed on the ground | A small rock travelling in space | A planet seen at night | A streak of light that glows in the air
exercise: «The streak of light burned across the night sky and vanished.» What is the streak of light? | *A meteor | A meteorite | A meteorite crater | An asteroid
exercise: «Vesta is the second most massive asteroid, and a giant impact on it blasted off rock that still falls to Earth as meteorites.» Where did those meteorites come from? | From the Earth's core | From the Earth's ocean floor | *From the asteroid Vesta | From the Sun
test: What is a meteoroid? | A giant hole in the ground | *A small rock travelling in space | A streak of light in our air | A piece of rock that has landed on the ground
test: Which phrase describes a meteorite that is heavy because it contains iron? | meteorite impact | asteroid belt | *iron meteorite | meteorite crater
exam: A meteor glows as a streak of light in the sky, and a piece of it later lands on the ground. What is that piece called? | Asteroid | Meteor | *Meteorite | Meteoroid
